  "conventions": [
    "Parameters b and k are real.",
    "Root counts below mean distinct real x values, not algebraic multiplicity.",
    "A positive root z of the auxiliary equation yields two distinct real roots x=+-sqrt(z). z=0 yields one real x=0; a negative or nonreal z yields no real x.",
    "The degree-four polynomials always have four complex roots counted with multiplicity. This is distinct from the exercise's real-root counting."
  ],
  "exercises": [
    {
      "number": "1060",
      "source_excerpt": "1060. 已知方程 $x^4-13x^2-k=0$ 有：а) 四个根； б) 两个根。求 $k$ 取值的集合。$k$ 是什么数时，方程有三个根？方程能不能只有一个根或一个根也没有？",
      "shared_derivation": [
        "Set z=x^2>=0. The auxiliary equation is z^2-13z-k=0, with discriminant D=169+4k, root sum 13, and root product -k.",
        "For k<-169/4, D<0, so no real z and no real x.",
        "For k=-169/4, the sole distinct z=13/2 is positive and repeated. The quartic is (x^2-13/2)^2, giving exactly two distinct real roots, each of multiplicity two.",
        "For -169/4<k<0, D>0, sum positive and product positive, so both distinct z roots are positive and yield four distinct real x values.",
        "For k=0, z is 0 or 13. The quartic is x^2(x^2-13), giving exactly three distinct real roots 0,+sqrt(13),-sqrt(13); zero has multiplicity two.",
        "For k>0, D>0 and product negative, so exactly one z root is positive and the other negative; exactly two distinct real x values result.",
        "The preceding cases exhaust all real k; no case has only one distinct real x. Evenness would require any nonzero root to have its distinct negative partner, and the only zero-root case also has +-sqrt(13)."
      ],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1060a",
          "source_label": "а",
          "requested": "k set for four distinct real roots",
          "conclusion": "-169/4<k<0",
          "root_formula": "x=+-sqrt((13+sqrt(169+4k))/2), +-sqrt((13-sqrt(169+4k))/2)",
          "domain": "Both radicands strictly positive and unequal."
        },
        {
          "id": "1060b",
          "source_label": "б",
          "requested": "k set for exactly two distinct real roots",
          "conclusion": "k=-169/4 or k>0",
          "branches": [
            {
              "condition": "k=-169/4",
              "roots": "+-sqrt(13/2)",
              "multiplicity_each": 2
            },
            {
              "condition": "k>0",
              "roots": "+-sqrt((13+sqrt(169+4k))/2)",
              "multiplicity_each": 1
            }
          ],
          "excluded_boundary": "k=0 gives three distinct real roots, not two."
        },
        {
          "id": "1060-three",
          "source_label": null,
          "requested": "k values for exactly three distinct real roots",
          "conclusion": "k=0",
          "roots": ["-sqrt(13)", "0", "sqrt(13)"],
          "zero_root_multiplicity": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "1060-one",
          "source_label": null,
          "requested": "whether exactly one distinct real root is possible",
          "conclusion": "No real k.",
          "reason": "Nonzero roots come in pairs. The only possible singleton would be zero, but k=0 also gives +-sqrt(13)."
        },
        {
          "id": "1060-none",
          "source_label": null,
          "requested": "whether no real root is possible",
          "conclusion": "Yes, exactly when k<-169/4.",
          "reason": "The auxiliary discriminant is then negative."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "1061",
      "source_excerpt": "1061. 已知方程 $x^4+bx^2+4=0$ 有四个根，求 $k$ 取值的集合。方程能不能只有两个根或一个根也没有？",
      "source_caveat": "The polynomial contains b, while the requested set names k. No relationship between b and k is supplied. Preserve both names; do not substitute k for b or invent an erratum.",
      "shared_derivation": [
        "For the actual polynomial set z=x^2>=0, obtaining z^2+bz+4=0. Its discriminant is b^2-16, root sum -b, root product 4.",
        "For b<-4, there are two distinct positive auxiliary roots and four distinct real x roots.",
        "For b=-4, the polynomial is (x^2-2)^2, so there are exactly two distinct real roots +-sqrt(2), each repeated twice.",
        "For -4<b<4, the auxiliary discriminant is negative. For b>=4, real auxiliary roots, when present, are negative because their sum is negative and product positive. Hence no real x for any b>-4.",
        "The constant term is 4, so zero is never a root. Evenness then precludes one or three distinct real roots.",
        "The actual coefficient classification constrains b. It does not identify k or repair the question asking for k."
      ],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1061-four",
          "source_label": null,
          "requested": "k set given four roots of the b polynomial",
          "status": "SOURCE_PARAMETER_MISMATCH",
          "actual_polynomial_condition": "b<-4 for four distinct real roots.",
          "conclusion": "No k constraint is supplied. If k is treated as a separate free real variable, every real k is compatible with a fixed b<-4; that is not a justified identification k=b.",
          "conditional_intended_parameter_answer": "Only if the question is separately clarified to ask for b, the set is b<-4.",
          "root_formula_for_actual_b": "x=+-sqrt((-b+sqrt(b^2-16))/2), +-sqrt((-b-sqrt(b^2-16))/2)"
        },
        {
          "id": "1061-two",
          "source_label": null,
          "requested": "whether the actual polynomial can have exactly two distinct real roots",
          "conclusion": "Yes, precisely at b=-4.",
          "roots": ["-sqrt(2)", "sqrt(2)"],
          "multiplicity_each": 2,
          "k_relation": "Not supplied."
        },
        {
          "id": "1061-none",
          "source_label": null,
          "requested": "whether the actual polynomial can have no real roots",
          "conclusion": "Yes, precisely when b>-4.",
          "k_relation": "Not supplied."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
